---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import education from "../assets/photos/education.jpg";
import teri from "../assets/photos/teri.jpg";
import ambassadors from "../assets/photos/ambassadors.jpg";

const pillars = [
  "Higher education",
  "Sporting excellence",
  "Goan culture",
  "Environmental conservation",
  "Affirmative action",
  "Health and sanitation",
];
---

<Base
  title="Sustainability and CSR"
  description="Dempo corporate social responsibility as published: education trusts, scholarships, Dempo Vishwa Gramshala, TERI programmes, and goodwill ambassadors in sport."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
      <span class="kicker">Sustainability</span>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); max-width: 14ch">People and planet, written into the house.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 1rem">
        The CSR page says decades of work with communities, mainly in Goa, made People and
        Planet second nature in the pursuit of Profit, and that the Group goes beyond the
        law in corporate citizenship. A population figure for Goa on the About page is
        undated, so it is not repeated. [Placeholder: client to confirm]
      </p>
      <ul class="pillars">
        {pillars.map((pillar) => <li>{pillar}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap split" data-reveal>
      <figure class="figure">
        <Image
          src={education}
          alt="Students and a campus scene from the Dempo Charities Trust photography on dempos.com."
          widths={[500, 900]}
          sizes="(min-width: 800px) 46vw, 100vw"
        />
        <figcaption>Dempo Charities Trust, as published on the CSR page.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="kicker">Dempo Charities Trust</span>
        <h2>Commitment to excellence, and quality education for all.</h2>
        <p>
          That is the motto on the trust’s page. The trust manages four institutions,
          affiliated to the Goa Board and Goa University:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Dhempe College of Arts and Science, Miramar, established 1962.</li>
          <li>Srinivassa Sinai Dempo College of Commerce & Economics, established 1966, with a campus the news pages place at Cujira.</li>
          <li>Vasantrao Dempo Higher Secondary School of Arts & Science, Miramar, 1975.</li>
          <li>Voicuntrao Sinai Dempo Higher Secondary School of Commerce, Miramar, 1975.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The trust page says scholarships and financial assistance reach hundreds of
          students, and that twenty-five scholarships were instituted in memory of
          Vasantrao Sinai Dempo for students from Santa Cruz, the ancestral village.
          The rupee total printed beside that aid is undated and is not repeated.
          [Placeholder: client to confirm] It also supports music, theatre and festivals
          of Goan tradition.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Vasudeva V. Dempo Memorial Lecture Series has had, as guest orators, the
          country’s former prime minister, the head of its largest private bank, and the head
          of its largest private steel company. The page does not name them.
        </p>
        <p>
          A separate Dempo Higher Secondary School of Science Trust runs an integrated board
          and competitive-exam model with IIT-ians PACE at the Miramar complex, described as
          Dempo PACE.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap prose" data-reveal>
      <span class="kicker">Scholarships, 2026–27</span>
      <h2 style="color: white">Dempo Charities Trust scholarships</h2>
      <p>
        The scheme supports meritorious Goan students in postgraduate, research or
        professional programmes in Goa or at institutions of repute elsewhere in India.
        Students enrolled in foreign colleges are not eligible, nor is anyone already
        holding another scholarship or freeship. Up to half the scholarships are earmarked
        for girl students. The amount covers tuition fee, in full or in part.
      </p>
      <p>
        The 2026 notice says the scheme is notified on 27 September 2026, with online
        applications from 27 September to 10 October 2026. Family-income papers refer to
        2025–26, with a threshold of ₹5 lakh a year between a government income certificate
        and income-tax returns. Rajesh R. Bhatikar signs as administrator.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lists of recipients for 2023, 2024 and 2025 are published on dempos.com as images.
        They are not retyped here.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.dempos.com/dempo-charities-trust-scholarships-2026/">2026 scheme</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://www.dempos.com/list-of-recipients-of-dct-scholarships-2025/">2025 recipients</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://www.dempos.com/list-of-recipients-of-dct-scholarships-2024/">2024 recipients</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://www.dempos.com/list-of-recipients-dct-scholarships-2023/">2023 recipients</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split" data-reveal>
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="kicker">Schools</span>
        <h2>Dempo Vishwa Gramshala</h2>
        <p>
          Dempo Vishwa Gramshala is an educational programme of the Vasantrao Dempo
          Education & Research Foundation, run with the Directorate of Education. A
          three-year engagement from 2023 with Government High School Kasarpal and
          Government High School Sal has been completed. A further adoption, under an MoU
          signed in March 2026, covers Government High School Kirlawada, Chimbel, and Ideal
          High School, Piligao, for 2026–2029.
        </p>
        <span class="kicker" style="margin-top: 2rem">Research</span>
        <h2>Vasantrao Dempo Education & Research Foundation</h2>
        <p>
          The CSR page describes Dempo Research Fellowships for Goa-centric study, with two
          books published — Kaleidoscope Goa, an encyclopaedia of Goan art and culture, and
          The Goan Village Communes, on the communidades — and a third in progress at the
          time of writing. It also describes an ethnographic project on rural Goa, with
          particular relevance to women, children, health and civil governance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="figure">
        <Image
          src={teri}
          alt="Students in a TERI and Dempo environmental education activity."
          widths={[500, 900]}
          sizes="(min-width: 800px) 46vw, 100vw"
        />
        <figcaption>TERI and Dempo, from the CSR page.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap split" data-reveal>
      <figure class="figure">
        <Image
          src={ambassadors}
          alt="Dempo goodwill ambassadors in sport, from the Group CSR photography."
          widths={[500, 900]}
          sizes="(min-width: 800px) 46vw, 100vw"
        />
        <figcaption>Goodwill ambassadors page on dempos.com. Ages printed there are not repeated, because the page is undated.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="kicker">Sport and climate</span>
        <h2>Ambassadors, TERI, and older gifts.</h2>
        <p>
          Dempo Goodwill Ambassadors, a scheme introduced by the chairman, has supported
          Natasha Palha in lawn tennis, Anurag Mhamal in chess and Tanisi Kirtani in table
          tennis. Past support named on the page includes Ivana Furtado in chess, Talasha
          Prabhu in swimming and Akanksha Salunkhe in squash. Ages printed on that undated
          page are not repeated. Goa Carbon has supported Bhakti Kulkarni in chess, and in
          June 2025 named badminton player Aarush Pawaskar a goodwill ambassador.
        </p>
        <p>
          With The Energy and Resources Institute, the Group launched the Vasudeva V. Dempo
          Climate Change Awareness Programme in 2010, for students and teachers from thirty
          schools. Project STARS — Sustainability Tracking, Action and Reporting in Schools —
          followed in August 2013, a three-year programme with ten schools. A later note on
          the site says the three-year project came to a close.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Group has also partnered the Confederation of Indian Industry on affirmative
          action for professional study among underprivileged communities.
        </p>
        <p>
          A 2000 account records a Vasudeva V. Dempo Conference Centre at the Goa Institute
          of Management, costing Rs 10.20 lakh and borne by V. S. Dempo & Co., and gifts of
          Rs 12 lakh each — Rs 24 lakh in all — to the Rotary Foundation in memory of
          Vaikunthrao Dempo and Vasudeva V. Dempo. The second endowment was created by
          Shrinivas V. Dempo with his mother, Neela V. Dempo.
        </p>
        <h3>Policies and filings</h3>
        <p>
          CSR policies are published for V. S. Dempo Holdings, Dempo Shipbuilding &
          Engineering, and Dempo Industries, plus a Dempo Industries CSR project note for
          2025–26. Annual returns for 2023–24 and 2024–25 are posted for Dempo Industries,
          Dempo Sports Club, V. S. Dempo Holdings, and Dempo Shipbuilding & Engineering.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.dempos.com/csr/">CSR</a>
          ·
          <a href="https://www.dempos.com/csr/csr-policies/">Policies</a>
          ·
          <a href="https://www.dempos.com/csr/statutory-filings/">Statutory filings</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
